mediawall is a small command line tool that works out a TV wall job:
the 16:9 screen size, the seating distance range (40 degree THX to 30
degree SMPTE field of view) and the field of view at your seat, the TV
mount heights, the recess (niche) rough opening, HDMI cable lengths
rounded up to stock sizes, slat wall panels to order and a materials
checklist. Output is plain text or JSON (--json). All lengths are in
inches.

Example:

  mediawall tv_diagonal=75 eye_height=44 seat_distance=110 \
    recessed=1 wall_type=brick soundbar=1

Run "mediawall" with no arguments for the list of keys.

The program has no crate dependencies, so the build is fully offline.
It needs a newer Rust than Slackware 15.0 ships, hence rust-opt.

NOTE:
  The program and this script were written with AI assistance and tested
by the GetMediaWall team, who maintain them.
